messages:
Nora H: FYI I repro'd a tiny duplicated tail when resuming streams in the browser SDK after token refresh. Only 3-5 chars but it breaks UI diffs.

Lee S: Which runtime? polyfill or native EventSource?

Nora H: Polyfill on Chrome. Native doesn't show it. Steps: start stream, wait for short JWT to expire, SDK refresh reconnects, resumed payload begins with 3-5 chars from previous chunk.

Pat G: Likely parse buffer retention across reconnects. Our polyfill keeps partial parse state so mid-chunk closures can leave a tail that gets replayed on resume.

Nora H: Parse loop excerpt:
```
let buf = '';
es.onmessage = (e) => {
  buf += e.data;
  const blocks = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = blocks.pop() || '';
  for (const b of blocks) handleEvent(b);
}
// reconnect currently preserves buf
```

Lee S: Quick fix: clear buf on reconnect. Longer term: standardize resume semantics (exclusive offsets) and add client dedupe by seq id.

infra-bot: note - staging nginx keepalive_timeout=60s; mid-chunk closes observed under load.

Pat G: I'll add a small PR to clear parser buffer on reconnect + a config flag resumeMode=(\"exclusive\"|\"inclusive\") defaulting to exclusive. Also add unit simulating TCP close mid-chunk.

Nora H: thanks. Ops please add nginx example and keepalive recommendations so we avoid mid-chunk kills.

Lee S: Also consider server heartbeats (":hb\n\n") so proxies don't close idle connections. Ensure client ignores them and they're not counted for billing.

Nora H: filing issue with repro and traces, will open PR tomorrow. Closing once CI green. :white_check_mark:
